    <fr:title text="Lambek's Syntactic Calculus">Lambek's Syntactic Calculus</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Lambek's <html:em>syntactic calculus</html:em> comprise the following rules:

<html:ul><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x \to  x]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(xy) z \to  x (yz)]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x (y z) \to  (xy) z]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[xy \to  z]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x \to  z/y]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[xy \to  z]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y \to  x \backslash  z]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x \to  z/y]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[xy \to  z]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y \to  x \backslash  z]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[xy \to  z]]></fr:tex></html:li>
  <html:li>if <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x \to  y]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y \to  z]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x \to  z]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ul></html:p>
    <html:p>Put by Lambek:
<html:blockquote>The system presented above may be viewed abstractly as a formal language with a number of primitive type symbols...</html:blockquote></html:p>
    <html:p>This description rings true, as we can read this as a very simple for type system for grammars that is later made more precise by <fr:link href="/dougherty-1993/" title="Closed Categories and Categorial Grammar" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/dougherty-1993/" display-uri="dougherty-1993" type="local">Dougherty</fr:link>.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
