                <fr:title text="Cut in the Syntactic Calculus">Cut in the Syntactic Calculus</fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>If <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T \to  x]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U , x , V \to  y]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U , T , V \to  y]]></fr:tex>.

Gentzen's theorem shows that this rule does not increase the expressivity of the deductive system.</html:p>
